  "id": "dsa-406",
  "title": "Height of a complete binary tree (or Heap) with N nodes - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider a </span><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-401\"><span>Binary Heap</span></a><span> of size N. Determine the height of the heap.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Examples:</strong></b></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Input :</strong></b><span> N = 6</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"tree\" height=\"312\" src=\"./images/dsa-406-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151713227555/tree.webp 390w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151713227555/tree-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151713227555/tree-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151713227555/tree-300.webp 300w\" width=\"390\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output :</strong></b><span> 2</span><br><b><strong>Explanation:</strong></b><span> The height of a tree is the number of edges on the longest path from root to leaf. Here, the longest path (e.g., 1 - 3 - 5) has 2 edges, so the tree’s height is 2.</span><br><span> </span><br><b><strong>Input :</strong></b><span> N = 9</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"ttree\" height=\"408\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/dsa-406-img-2.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151839424736/ttree.webp 528w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151839424736/ttree-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151839424736/ttree-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260203151839424736/ttree-300.webp 300w\" width=\"528\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output :</strong></b><span> 3</span><br><b><strong>Explanation:</strong></b><span> In this tree the longest path (e.g., 2 - 3 - 5 - 6) has 3 edges, so the tree’s height is 3.</span></p></blockquote></div><a id=\"practiceBanner\" class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_practiceDivBanner__idAxy ArticlePracticeBanner_desktopOnly__r87aW rc0\" href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/height-of-heap5025/1\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"display:block\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><div class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_recommendedDiv__7Q5go\">Try It Yourself<div class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_icon__UeNv9\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/dsa-406-img-3.svg\" alt=\"redirect icon\" class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_redirectIcon__mJJ_m undefined\"></div></div></a><div class=\"html-chunk\"><h3 id=\"approach-using-mathematical-formula-o1-time-and-o1-space\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>[Approach] Using Mathematical Formula - O(1) Time and O(1) Space</span></h3><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Since a binary heap is a </span><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-892\"><span>complete binary tree</span></a><span>, its height is found using the formula floor(log</span><sub><span>2</span></sub><span>N).</span></p></blockquote><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C++</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"cpp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-cpp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">std</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">floor</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">log2</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Java</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"java\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-java\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.lang.*</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">GFG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">ceil</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Python</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"python3\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-python3\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"nn\">math</span>\n<span class=\"k\">def</span> <span class=\"nf\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">math</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ceil</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">math</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">log2</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">))</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">N</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">6</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C#</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"csharp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-csharp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">System</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">GFG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ceiling</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">                   </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">6</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">JavaScript</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">N</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">ceil</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">2</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// Driver Code    </span>\n<span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">6</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">height</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">N</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><div class=\"code-output\"><br><strong>Output</strong><pre>2</pre></div></div>",
  "textContent": "Consider a Binary Heap of size N. Determine the height of the heap.Examples:Input : N = 6 Output : 2Explanation: The height of a tree is the number of edges on the longest path from root to leaf. Here, the longest path (e.g., 1 - 3 - 5) has 2 edges, so the tree’s height is 2. Input : N = 9 Output : 3Explanation: In this tree the longest path (e.g., 2 - 3 - 5 - 6) has 3 edges, so the tree’s height is 3.Try It Yourself[Approach] Using Mathematical Formula - O(1) Time and O(1) SpaceSince a binary heap is a complete binary tree, its height is found using the formula floor(log2N).\n            C++\n\n    #include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint height(int N)\n{\n    return floor(log2(N));\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n    int N = 6;\n    cout << height(N);\n    return 0;\n}\n\n\n            Java\n\n    import java.lang.*;\n\nclass GFG {\n    \n    static int height(int N)\n    {\n        return (int)Math.ceil(Math.log(N + 1) / Math.log(2)) - 1;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args)\n    {\n        int N = 6;\n        System.out.println(height(N));\n    }\n}\n\n\n            Python\n\n    import math\ndef height(N):\n    return math.ceil(math.log2(N + 1)) - 1\n\nN = 6\nprint(height(N))\n\n\n            C#\n\n    using System;\n\nclass GFG {\n    static int height(int N)\n    {\n        return (int)Math.Ceiling(Math.Log(N \n                   + 1) / Math.Log(2)) - 1;\n    }\n\n    public static void Main()\n    {\n        int N = 6;\n        Console.Write(height(N));\n    }\n}\n\n\n            JavaScript\n\n    function height(N)\n{\n    return Math.ceil(Math.log(N + 1) / Math.log(2)) - 1;\n}\n    \n// Driver Code    \nlet N = 6;\nconsole.log(height(N));\n\nOutput2",
